job_description:
About the job

Job Description

Melaksanakan kegiatan layanan transaksi keuangan digital sebagai fungsi CS & Teller;
Melaksanakan kegiatan operasional harian, umum & logistik, dan SDM;
Memberikan layanan atas kebutuhan informasi produk maupun keluhan nasabah;
Melaksanakan pengelolaan dan administrasi transaksi layanan, operasional, umum & logistik, dan SDM

Requirement

Calon Pekerja diutamakan dari wilayah setempat
Bersedia ditempatkan di Community Branch Yogyakarta Bank Raya
Berpenampilan menarik, komunikatif dan persuasif;
Berorientasi pada ketelitian dan kepuasan nasabah;
Minimal D3 dari semua fakultas/jurusan terakreditasi minimal B.
Perguruan Tinggi Negeri/Perguruan Tinggi Swasta dengan Indeks Prestasi Kumulatif (lPK) minimal 3,00 (skala 4).
Mampu mengoperasikan gadget (smartphone, dsb) serta komputer dengan baik (minimal MS. Office, Excel dan Power Point)

About the job

Job Requirements:

Minimum Bachelor’s degree (S1), preferably in Economics, Finance, Accounting, or related fields;
At least 1 year of experience as an Equity Research Analyst (consumer/retail coverage is a plus);
Strong financial modeling and valuation skills;
Solid understanding of financial statements and capital markets;
Proficiency in Excel; familiarity with Bloomberg or similar platforms is an advantage;
Strong analytical thinking and attention to detail;
Good written and verbal communication skills in English;
Ability to work under tight deadlines and manage multiple tasks; and
Having a Capital Market License (WPPE) is preferred.




Job Descriptions:

In-depth Research: Conduct thorough research, analyzing earnings releases, regulatory filings, and relevant news events to derive actionable insights;
Financial Modeling and Valuation: Develop complex financial models to understand industry dynamics and perform detailed valuation analyses. Prepare research notes and sector reports;
Communication: Engage with internal and external clients as well as management teams, providing expert opinions and updates on stocks and the sector;
Client Coverage: Work closely with partners in sales and trading to ensure comprehensive client coverage, responding to client inquiries and providing updates on market conditions and insights.







About Us

Mirae Asset Sekuritas Indonesia as Permanent Innovator upholds a philosophy centered on long-term relationships, integrity, and client-focused innovation. Guided by our Business Philosophy, Vision and Core Values—Client First, Objectivity, Teamwork, and Citizenship—we strive to provide comprehensive and transparent financial services that empower our clients to achieve sustainable growth. Our commitment is to continuously evolve, delivering value-added services that anticipate and adapt to the changing needs of our clients in capital market industry.




Join us to be part of a team where your professional journey is enriched by shared values and a dedication to excellence.

About the job

About UOB

United Overseas Bank Limited (UOB) is a leading bank in Asia with a global network of more than 500 branches and offices in 19 countries and territories in Asia Pacific, Europe and North America. In Asia, we operate through our head office in Singapore and banking subsidiaries in China, Indonesia, Malaysia and Thailand, as well as branches and offices. Our history spans more than 80 years. Over this time, we have been guided by our values – Honorable, Enterprising, United and Committed. This means we always strive to do what is right, build for the future, work as one team and pursue long-term success. It is how we work, consistently, be it towards the company, our colleagues or our customers.

Job Description


Responsible for the preparation and the execution of Corporate Action namely AGM/EGM, Capital Injection, Bonds Issuance;
Responsible for reporting to OJK, LPS, KSEI and other authorized parties, related to the management and corporate actions;
Responsible for preparing and coordinating the issuance of Annual Report, ensuring the adherence with the prevailing regulations, as well as submitting to the regulators;
Responsible for preparing GCG implementation reports and GCG Self-Assessment for section/factor related to BOC, BOD and BOC's Committees; Assisting the Independent Commissioners and BOC Committee (Audit Committee, and ICG Committee) in terms of arranging the meeting schedule and ensure that the Meeting fulfill the quorum for decision making; Drafting the MOM to be reviewed by respective presenters and committee members; ensuring that Independent Commissioners obtain the updated and adequate information regarding the condition and situation of the Bank;
Preparing the monthly reports to the Board of Commissioners which consist of information related to BOC, to be reviewed by the CST Head and Compliance, Legal & Corporate Secretary Director, and endorsed by President Director;
Assisting CST Head to prepare manual updates for BOD, BOC, BOC's Committees and Executive Committees in accordance with the prevailing regulations;
Assisting CST Head to review and update SOP in CST at least once a year or if necessary; Review deeds, agreements and other corporate legal documents to ensure that it is in accordance with prevailing regulations;
Provide advice and input to other units related to Bank’s information, corporate governance, legal documentation, etc.;
Carrying out other tasks assigned by CST Head and Management.


Additional Requirements

Be a Part of the UOB Family

UOB is an equal opportunity employer. UOB does not discriminate on the basis of a candidate's age, race, gender, color, religion, sexual orientation, physical or mental disability, or other non-merit factors. All employment decisions at UOB are based on business needs, job requirements and qualifications. If you require any assistance or accommodations to be made for the recruitment process, please inform us when you submit your online application.

Apply now and make a Difference
